cff-version: 1.2.0
message: If you use this app, please cite it and the works it builds on, listed under references.
type: software
title: eeg-connectivity
abstract: Sensor-space functional connectivity of clinical scalp EEG (routine and long-term video-EEG), one step of the
  Scalp EEG Interictal Biomarkers workflow. The weighted phase lag index (default) and the imaginary part of coherency
  (mne-connectivity spectral_connectivity_epochs, multitaper, 4 s artifact-free epochs outside seizures) and the
  orthogonalised amplitude envelope correlation (mne-connectivity envelope_correlation) per frequency band, all
  insensitive to zero-lag volume conduction; node strength; graph measures with networkx (weighted clustering,
  characteristic path length, global efficiency, Louvain modularity, small-worldness against degree-preserving null
  networks) on proportionally thresholded networks; hemispheric means and asymmetry as a sensor-level proxy of the
  network asymmetry studied in temporal lobe epilepsy. Works on referential recordings (in average reference) and on
  bipolar-only recordings (with a warning). Research outputs, to be reviewed by a clinician.
authors:
